      "id": "D1",
      "title": "Atomic Lifetime Click Increment via ExecuteUpdateAsync",
      "choice": "Use EF Core's SetProperty ExecuteUpdateAsync on ShortLinks matching Id to increment ClickCount (s => s.ClickCount + 1) and set LastVisitedAtUtc directly in SQLite.",
      "rationale": "Prevents lost updates caused by concurrent in-memory read-modify-write operations while keeping EF Core change tracking clean and minimal.",
      "alternatives": [
        "Read-modify-write with EF Core optimistic concurrency tokens (RowVersion/ConcurrencyCheck), rejected because concurrent updates would throw exceptions and fail redirects.",
        "Raw SQL UPDATE statement, rejected because ExecuteUpdateAsync provides type safety and translates directly to an atomic SQLite UPDATE."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "title": "Atomic Daily Analytics Upsert via Raw SQLite ON CONFLICT",
      "choice": "Execute a raw SQL query `INSERT INTO ShortLinkDailyClicks (ShortLinkId, Date, Clicks) VALUES (@linkId, @date, 1) ON CONFLICT(ShortLinkId, Date) DO UPDATE SET Clicks = ShortLinkDailyClicks.Clicks + 1` via Database.ExecuteSqlInterpolatedAsync.",
      "rationale": "SQLite natively supports ON CONFLICT clauses; a single atomic query guarantees no race conditions or duplicate key violations under high concurrency without requiring in-memory locking.",
      "alternatives": [
        "Query first, then insert or update in C#, rejected due to inherent race conditions under concurrent requests.",
        "Application-level SemaphoreSlim locking on link ID, rejected because it does not scale across instances and adds significant latency."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D3",
