      "choice": "Prior to calling Database.MigrateAsync(), execute an explicit transaction checking sqlite_master for legacy tables, creating missing tables with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS, ensuring __EFMigrationsHistory exists, and seeding the initial migration ID.",
      "rationale": "Prevents MigrateAsync from failing with 'table already exists' on legacy SQLite databases created with EnsureCreatedAsync, while guaranteeing atomicity if startup is interrupted.",
      "alternatives": [
        "Running Database.MigrateAsync() directly and catching SQLite exceptions, rejected because partial migration failures leave the database corrupted.",
        "Manual offline migration scripts, rejected because the service must self-heal and upgrade seamlessly upon startup."
      ]
